    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Explore a Chatbot\r\n\r\nThese levels let you experiment with chatbots. They use a language model behind the scenes to answer questions. Let's experiment and see what questions we can get answered.\r\n\r\n**Fair Warning:** This chatbot is for educational purposes, so we've built in appropriate restrictions and accountability to make sure it doesn't get abused. Inappropriate messages from you _or_ the chatbot will be flagged and not displayed. The chatbot also keeps track of **all messages you send to it**, and your teacher can view these messages (even the ones that were flagged as inappropriate). So be sure to just use the chatbot as directed!\r\n\r\n### Do This\r\n\r\n1) Ask the chatbot 3-4 questions. Try to determine its purpose.\r\n2) Find the button that lets you clear the chat. This also resets the conversation\r\n3) Find the button that lets you copy the chat. This will be useful to know about later!\r\n\r\nTest the chatbot! Have a conversation with at least 4 messages, then press the <code style=\"color:white; background-color:#7435b2\">Continue</code> button!\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n::: details [**Click here to see example messages to try in this level**]\r\n* What is space like?\r\n* Where is Tucson located?\r\n* Where can I get a good chile relleno?\r\n:::\r\n\r\n&nbsp;",
